(--muted)">About $315</td><td data-label="Resale homes usually sell for" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $535,000</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Community" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/del-webb-grande-dunes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Del Webb at Grande Dunes</a></td><td data-label="Area" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach</td><td data-label="Minutes to the beach by car" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 4</td><td data-label="HOA fee a month" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $400 for a house</td><td data-label="Resale homes usually sell for" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $665,000 for a house</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Community" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/myrtle-trace/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Myrtle Trace</a></td><td data-label="Area" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Conway</td><td data-label="Minutes to the beach by car" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 15</td><td data-label="HOA fee a month" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$95</td><td data-label="Resale homes usually sell for" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $300,000</td></tr><tr><td data-label="Community" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)"><a href="/buyers/55-plus-communities/seasons-at-prince-creek-west/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Seasons at Prince Creek West</a></td><td data-label="Area" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Murrells Inlet</td><td data-label="Minutes to the beach by car" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 13</td><td data-label="HOA fee a month" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $340</td><td data-label="Resale homes usually sell for" style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About $500,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="what-are-the-pros-and-cons-of-living-in-del-webb-north"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Pros and cons">What are the pros and cons of living in Del Webb North Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Del Webb North Myrtle Beach has new homes about a mile from the ocean, and the builder is still selling them.</p><style>.c3-pc{display:grid;gap:1rem;max-width:960px;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem}@media (min-width:760px){.c3-pc{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start}}.c3-pc>div{padding:1.1rem 1.2rem .6rem}.c3-pc h3{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .8rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem}.c3-pc,.c3-pc ul{font-size:1em}.c3-pc ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.c3-pc li{display:flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:flex-start;color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 .9rem}.c3-pc li svg{flex:none;margin-top:.3rem}.c3-pc .c3-pc-do{display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:500;margin-top:.2rem}</style><div class="c3-pc"><div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass)"><h3>Pros</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>The beach is about 4 minutes away by car.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>The homes are new, built since 2022.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>If you sell, the next owner keeps the builder's warranty on the structure.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>The city's community center, with indoor pickleball, is about a minute away by car.</span></li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--muted)"><h3>Cons</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>The builder is still building here. <span class="c3-pc-do">Ask which streets are finished before you choose a lot.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Golf carts may cross US 17 but not drive along it.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>The airport is about 35 minutes away by car.</span></li></ul></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="can-you-rent-out-a-home-in-del-webb-north-myrtle-beach"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Renting">Can you rent out a home in Del Webb North Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not by the week. Renters in Del Webb North Myrtle Beach must stay <a href="https://www.nmb.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Item/412?fileID=627" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">at least 30 days</a>.</p><div class="c3-story" style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:1.5rem 1.5rem .7rem;margin:1.4rem 0 1.4rem;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem"><strong>Example:</strong> Frank and Joyce plan to spend summers near their son in Michigan. While they are away, they want to rent their new house to vacationers by the week.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem">They pick out a new house in Del Webb North Myrtle Beach and are ready to sign the builder's contract. Before they sign, their Chapter3 agent reads the renting rules for the neighborhood with them.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem">Every renter there must stay at least 30 days, so they cannot rent by the week. Frank and Joyce plan on one renter for the whole summer, and they sign the contract.</p></div><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Tell us how you plan to use the home.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">An agent gets the HOA documents and reads the rental rules with you before you sign the builder's contract.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Talk to an agent</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="del-webb-north-myrtle-beach-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Del Webb North Myrtle Beach FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How much is the HOA fee in Del Webb North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The HOA fee is about $315 a month. It includes lawn care, internet and a TV package.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Del Webb North Myrtle Beach finished?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Not yet. The builder is still building and selling new houses in the neighborhood today.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can someone under 55 live in Del Webb North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes, a younger husband or wife can live in the home, as long as one person in the household is 55 or older.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Del Webb North Myrtle Beach inside the city limits?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. It is inside North Myrtle Beach, so owners pay a city tax on top of the county and school tax.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Who builds the homes in Del Webb North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Pulte builds them and sells them under its Del Webb name. Most of its homes here are one story, with a garage.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.delwebb.com/homes/south-carolina/myrtle-beach/north-myrtle-beach/del-webb-north-myrtle-beach-210691" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Del Webb North Myrtle Beach website</a>, <a href="https://www.nmb.us/AgendaCenter/ViewFile/Item/412?fileID=627" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">City agreement and plan for the neighborhood</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County tax levies</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County deed records</a>, <a href="https://msc.fema.gov/portal/search?AddressQuery=1285%20Possum%20Trot%20Road%2C%20North%20Myrtle%20Beach%2C%20SC%2029582" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA flood map</a>. This is not legal or tax advice, and builder prices change. The HOA fee and home sizes are from recent home listings. Drive times come from OpenStreetMap and leave out traffic. The flood cost is the middle FEMA price for policies in ZIP code 29582.</p><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Del Webb North Myrtle Beach from above. Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey, <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://noaa-eri-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html#2026_Pre_Event/EC2601a_OB_N_RGB/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA Emergency Response Imagery</a>. Chapter3 Realty joined four NOAA map tiles, drew the outline from Horry County GIS parcels, added one label and adjusted the colors.</div><div role="listitem">A street of homes in Del Webb North Myrtle Beach, with a pond and a walking path behind them. Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey, <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://noaa-eri-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html#2026_Pre_Event/EC2601a_OB_N_RGB/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA Emergency Response Imagery</a>. Chapter3 Realty joined four NOAA map tiles, cut a close view of one street and adjusted the colors.</div><div role="listitem">From the air: the beach, US 17 and Del Webb North Myrtle Beach. Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey, <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://noaa-eri-pds.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html#2026_Pre_Event/EC2601a_OB_N_RGB/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NOAA Emergency Response Imagery</a>. Chapter3 Realty cut this view from one NOAA aerial photo, resized it, adjusted the 