 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Myrtle Trace a gated community?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Only in part. The front entrance is always open. The HOA put gates on the back entrance so drivers do not cut through the neighborhood."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much is the HOA fee in Myrtle Trace?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The HOA fee is $95 a month. The HOA uses it to keep up the pool, the clubhouse, the gates, the roads it owns, the ponds and the shared land."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Myrtle Trace South part of Myrtle Trace?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Myrtle Trace South and Myrtle Trace Grande are separate neighborhoods, each with its own HOA. The fee and rules on this page are for Myrtle Trace."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who runs the Myrtle Trace HOA?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The owners run the Myrtle Trace HOA themselves, with volunteers. There is no management company."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the golf course part of Myrtle Trace?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Burning Ridge Golf Club, next door, is privately owned and is not part of the HOA. Some Myrtle Trace homes back onto it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you fish in the Myrtle Trace ponds?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Residents and their house guests can fish from the shared land around the 15 ponds. You let every fish go."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you need flood insurance in Myrtle Trace?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Probably not. No home here is in a high-risk flood zone. If you want a policy, it usually costs about $550 a year."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Myrtle Trace inside Conway city limits?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Myrtle Trace has a Conway mailing address but is outside the city, so owners there pay no Conway city tax."}}]}</script>
