040"/><path d="M46 134L130 66" fill="none" stroke="#1c2028" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M130 66Q150 92 152 124" fill="none" stroke="#5c6b78" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><circle cx="152" cy="125" r="3.5" fill="#c4783a"/><path d="M148.5 125a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 7 0Z" fill="#fbf8f2"/><rect x="54" y="140" width="16" height="10" rx="2" fill="#80b1bc"/><rect x="54" y="140" width="16" height="3" rx="1" fill="#fbf8f2"/><path d="M206 150V112M214 152V104M222 150V116M198 152V120" fill="none" stroke="#6f8f5f" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><ellipse cx="214" cy="104" rx="2.6" ry="7" fill="#91592b"/><ellipse cx="206" cy="112" rx="2.4" ry="6" fill="#91592b"/><ellipse cx="222" cy="116" rx="2.4" ry="6" fill="#91592b"/><path d="M196 152q8 -22 2 -40M228 154q-6 -18 0 -34" fill="none" stroke="#87a570" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><strong>Fishing</strong><span class="c3ph-t">Ponds where you and your guests fish and let the fish go. You cannot swim or take a boat in the ponds.</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">There is also line dancing, a coffee group and a craft fair.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-are-the-homes-like-in-myrtle-trace"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The homes">What are the homes like in Myrtle Trace?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most homes in Myrtle Trace are one-story houses with their own yards, and a few are townhouses. Most were built in the 1980s and 1990s.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most have 3 bedrooms and about 1,500 to 2,100 square feet. The houses are on curving streets among trees and ponds, with Burning Ridge Golf Club next door. Wide paths between the houses are open to every resident.</p><div class="c3-aerial"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/myrtle-trace-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/myrtle-trace-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/myrtle-trace-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="675" alt="Myrtle Trace from above, with its edge drawn in orange: houses among tall pines and ponds, the clubhouse and main entrance marked, and the golf course next door" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Myrtle Trace from above, with the golf course next door. The orange line is the edge of the neighborhood.</figcaption></figure></div><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/myrtle-trace-homes-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/myrtle-trace-homes-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/myrtle-trace-homes-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Houses with dark roofs, green yards and trees along two curving streets and a pond in Myrtle Trace, seen from above" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Houses along two streets and a pond in Myrtle Trace, from above.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Some homes look out on the golf course, which is privately owned. Golf balls from the course can land in those yards.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Each owner takes care of the house and the yard, including the roof and the grass.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get the list of Myrtle Trace homes for sale.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us what you are looking for, and one of our agents will send you the homes for sale now.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Get the list</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="what-is-conway-like"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Conway">What is Conway like?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Conway is the town next to Myrtle Trace, on the Waccamaw River. Main Street in Conway is about 10 minutes away by car. Conway's riverwalk is a wooden boardwalk along the water, shaded by trees.</p><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-riverwalk-boardwalk-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="900" alt="A wooden boardwalk with a black railing, shaded by trees, beside old wooden buildings in Conway" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pubdog. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: Pubdog</a></span></div><figcaption>The riverwalk in Conway.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Main Street is lined with old brick buildings with shops and places to eat.</p><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-main-street-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-main-street-600w.webp 600w, /images/55-plus/myrtle-trace/conway-main-street-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Main Street in downtown Conway, South Carolina, lined with old brick shop buildings" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pubdog. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: Pubdog</a></span></div><figcaption>Main Street in Conway.</figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-does-it-cost-to-live-in-myrtle-trace"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Costs">What does it cost to live in Myrtle Trace?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Homes in Myrtle Trace usually sell for about $300,000. If you live in the home, plan for these costs:</p><ul role="list" style="list-style:none;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(13rem,1fr));gap:.75rem;max-width:760px"><li style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.9rem .85rem 1rem;margin:0"><span style="display:flex;width:2.6rem;height:2.6rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory-2);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:.6rem"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M15 9.4c-.4-1-1.5-1.8-3-1.8-1.8 0-3 1-3 2.2 0 3 6 1.6 6 4.4 0 1.3-1.3 2.2-3 2.2-1.6 0-2.7-.7-3.1-1.8M12 5.8v1.8M12 16.4v1.8"/><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/></svg></span><strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:.25rem">HOA fee</strong><span style="display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5">$95 a month</span></li><li style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.9rem .85rem 1rem;margin:0"><span style="display:flex;width:2.6rem;height:2.6rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory-2);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:.6rem"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6 3h8l4 4v13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H6a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1zM14 3v4h4M9 17l6-6"/><circle cx="9.5" cy="11.5" r="1"/><circle cx="14.5" cy="16.5" r="1"/></svg></span><strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:.25rem">Property tax</strong><span style="display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5">About $1,200 a year</span></li><li style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.9rem .85rem 1rem;margin:0"><span style="display:flex;width:2.6rem;height:2.6rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory-2);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:.6rem"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:.25rem">When you buy</strong><span style="display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5">A one-time fee to the HOA of a little over $1,500</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The HOA uses the fee to keep up the pool, the clubhouse, the gates, the roads it owns, the ponds and the shared land. Myrtle Trace has a Conway address but is outside the city limits, so you pay no Conway city tax.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You probably will not need flood insurance, because no home here is in a high-risk flood zone on <a href="https://msc.fema.gov/portal/search?AddressQuery=101%20Myrtle%20Trace%20Drive%2C%20Conway%2C%20SC%2029526" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the government's flood map</a>. If you want it, a policy here usually costs about $550 a year.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Get an insurance quote before you offer.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Pick the Myrtle Trace home you like. An agent at Chapter3 helps you get a homeowners <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">insurance</a> quote before you write the offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Get a quote</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="who-can-live-in-myrtle-trace"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Who can live here">Who can live in Myrtle Trace?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At least one person in every home in Myrtle Trace must be 55 or older, under the <a href="https://myrtletracesc.org/wp-content/uploads/Guidelines/MyrtleTraceCovenant.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HOA's rules</a>. The others in the home can be any age, and grandchildren can visit.</p><ul role="list" style="list-style:none;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(18rem,1fr));gap:.75rem;max-width:760px"><li style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.9rem .85rem 1rem;margin:0"><span style="display:flex;width:2.6rem;height:2.6rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:.6rem"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 13c-2.5 0-5 2.6-5 5 0 1.6 1.2 2.5 2.6 2.5.9 0 1.6-.5 2.4-.5s1.5.5 2.4.5c1.4 0 2.6-.9 2.6-2.5 0-2.4-2.5-5-5-5z"/><circle cx="5.3" cy="11" r="1.8"/><circle cx="9" cy="6.3" r="1.8"/><circle cx="15" cy="6.3" r="1.8"/><circle cx="18.7" cy="11" r="1.8"/></svg></span><strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:.25rem">Pets</strong><span style="display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5">Yes. Keep them on a leash outside your yard, and out of the clubhouse and pool area.</span></li><li style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.9rem .85rem 1rem;margin:0"><span style="display:flex;width:2.6rem;height:2.6rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:.6rem"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10.8 12.2 20 3M16.8 6.2l2.5 2.5M14.3 8.7l2 2"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="4.5"/></svg></span><strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:.25rem">Renting it out</strong><span style="display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5">Yes, for a year or longer. One tenant must be 55 or older and live there.</span></li><li style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.9rem .85rem 1rem;margin:0"><span style="display:flex;width:2.6rem;height:2.6rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:.6rem"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 11.5 12 3.5l9 8M5.5 10v10.5h13V10M10 20.5V15h4v5.5"/></svg></span><strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:.25rem">Sheds and pools</strong><span style="display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5">No free-standing sheds, gazebos or private swimming pools.</span></li><li style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.9rem .85rem 1rem;margin:0"><span style="display:flex;width:2.6rem;height:2.6rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:.6rem"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 3v13M12 3l7 11h-7M10 6l-5 8h5M3 16h18l-2 4H5z"/></svg></span><strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:.25rem">Trucks and boats</strong><span style="display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5">Park your truck in the garage. Campers, boats and RVs can park at the clubhouse lot with a permit.</span></li></ul><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In our experience, many HOAs here do not allow renting at all. Myrtle Trace does.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="how-does-myrtle-trace-compare-with-other-55-neighborhoods"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Compare">How does Myrtle Trace compare with other 55+ neighborhoods?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Myrtle Trace has the lowest HOA fee of these four 55+ neighborhoods, and its homes usually sell for the least.</p><style>.c3-cmp tr.c3-self td{background:#fff;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy)!important}@media (max-width:599px){.c3-cmp tr.c3-self{background:#fff;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cmp tr.c3-self td{background:transparent}}@media (max-width:599px){.c3-cmp table,.c3-cmp tbody,.c3-cmp tr,.c3-cmp td{display:block;width:100%}.c3-cmp thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0)}.c3-cmp tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .75rem;padding:.4rem 0}.c3-cmp td{border:0!important;padding:.25rem .9rem!important}.c3-cmp td:first-child{color:var(--navy)!important;font-weight:500;font-size:1rem}.c3-cmp td[data-label]:not(:first-