+<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/buyers/">Buyers</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Homes With No HOA</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Buying a home</p><h1 class="detail-h1">Where can you buy a home with no HOA near Myrtle Beach?<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">16 areas where most homes have no fee.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated October 27, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">Room for a boat, a truck and a shed, from Little River to Aynor.</p></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Almost every house for sale outside a named subdivision is listed with no homeowners association (HOA) fee, and so are about three in four built before 1990. Most are in the areas below, from beach streets and river towns to country land.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="where"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The map and the guide">Where are they?</h2><style id="c3-glass">main#main{--g-ink:#8a5226;--g-ink-lg:#a8612c;--g-edge:rgba(255,255,255,.8);--g-hi:inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,.95);--g-sh:0 1px 2px rgba(28,32,40,.05),0 14px 36px -20px rgba(28,32,40,.3);--g-r:20px;--g-blur:saturate(150%) blur(16px);background-color:#f8f4e