+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/from-new-york/#article","headline":"Moving From New York to Myrtle Beach","description":"What changes moving from New York to the Grand Strand: income and property tax, what your sale buys here, the yearly vehicle tax, and the residency trap.","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/from-new-york/","author":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/about/#devin-day"},"reviewedBy":{"@type":"Person","name":"Timothy Nash","alternateName":"Tim Nash","jobTitle":"Broker-in-Charge"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/#org"},"datePublished":"2026-08-16","dateModified":"2026-10-27","inLanguage":"en-US","image":"https://chapter3realty.com/og-image.jpg","mainEntityOfPage":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/from-new-york/#webpage"},"about":{"@type":"Thing","name":"Moving From New York to Myrtle Beach"},"keywords":"moving from New York to Myrtle Beach, New York to South Carolina relocation, NY to Myrtle Beach taxes"}</script>
 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/from-new-york/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much cheaper is Myrtle Beach than New York?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Overall prices are about 17 percent lower than the New York metro area on the federal price index, and housing about 44 percent lower. In July 2026 the typical home was about $342,000 here against about $737,000 there. A household earning $95,000 in the New York metro keeps the same standard of living here on about $79,000."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will my property taxes go down if I move from New York to South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"From Long Island, Westchester or Rockland, substantially. Those counties run effective rates of roughly 1.6 to 2.1 percent, against about 0.38 percent in Horry County on a primary home. From Brooklyn, Queens or Staten Island, much less: the boroughs average 0.56 to 0.88 percent because assessment caps hold assessed values well below market, so the gap is far smaller."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does South Carolina tax my pension if I move from New York?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often, yes. New York fully exempts New York State and local government pensions, federal pensions and military pensions, with no cap. South Carolina exempts military retirement fully, but a state or municipal pension from New York becomes taxable here beyond the retirement and age-65 deductions. Social Security is untaxed in both states."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I have to pay tax on my car every year in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, and New York does not do this, so it surprises people. Vehicles are assessed at 6 percent of value at the full local rate, so a $30,000 car is taxed roughly $360 a year outside the city limits. You also pay a one-time $250 fee per vehicle when you first register it here, and you have 45 days from moving to do it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can New York still tax me after I move to South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It can, in two situations. New York says your domicile does not change until you can show with clear and convincing evidence that you abandoned it. Separately, even with a genuine domicile change, New York taxes you as a full-year resident if you keep a permanent home there for substantially all of the year and spend 184 days or more in the state. Keeping the old house and visiting family half the year is the common trap. Get advice from a tax professional before you plan your year."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the biggest cost that goes up when moving from New York?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Insurance. A coastal policy here is often homeowners plus wind and hail plus flood, priced separately, with hurricane deductibles set as a percentage of the insured value. Get an insurance quote before you write an offer, because it changes the monthly number more than any other line."}}]}</script>
