 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/from-north-carolina/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Myrtle Beach cheaper than North Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Close, and it depends on the line. Houses cost less than Charlotte or Raleigh, groceries lose the 2 percent tax, gas is about 12 cents cheaper, and property tax is lower. Income tax is lower only below about $100,000 of joint income. The calculator on our cost of living page runs your exact city."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will my property taxes go down if I move from North Carolina to South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, on average. Charlotte and Raleigh average about 0.69 percent effective while Horry County averages about 0.38 percent on a primary home, and the primary rate also removes the school operating tax. Expect a saving of a few thousand a year on a comparable house, not a windfall."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does South Carolina tax my North Carolina pension?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It depends which pension. Military retirement is exempt in both states. Some older North Carolina government pensions are fully exempt there and taxed here past the deductions, so that group should run the numbers first. Private pensions and 401(k)s usually do better here, because South Carolina has retirement deductions and North Carolina has none."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the vehicle tax different in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The idea is the same: both states tax cars yearly with the plate. The mechanics differ here: the county bills you before the plate renews, a car titled elsewhere pays a one-time $250 fee, and you have 45 days from the move to register."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much do homes cost in Myrtle Beach compared with Charlotte or Raleigh?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A typical home here costs about $342,000, against about $389,000 in the Charlotte area and about $437,000 in the Raleigh area, on the same July 2026 measure."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why do so many people move from North Carolina to Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"More people move to Myrtle Beach from North Carolina than from anywhere else. The usual reasons are the coast itself, more house for the money than the Charlotte or Raleigh metros, and retirement deductions North Carolina does not offer. The bills are close. The coast is the difference."}}]}</script>
