 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/relocating/schools/#faq","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I find out which school an address is zoned for in Horry County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Use the district's Attendance Zone Lookup, which takes a street address and returns the assigned elementary, middle, and high school. If the address is new construction it may not return a result until the lot has a posted address. The district's helpdesk at 843-488-6825 answers zone questions, and the school's front office can confirm before you write an offer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do school attendance zones change in Horry County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, and recently. When two elementary schools opened in Carolina Forest, the district moved the lines for three existing elementary schools and published the list of subdivisions that changed. The rezoning took about four months from first draft to board vote, and the new lines took effect the following August. Never rely on the school names in a home's advertisement, and never assume this year's zone is next year's."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which school district serves Pawleys Island and Murrells Inlet?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It depends on the county line. Horry County Schools serves all of Horry County, which includes Myrtle Beach, North Myrtle Beach, Conway, Carolina Forest, Socastee, Surfside Beach, and the Horry side of Murrells Inlet. Georgetown County School District serves Pawleys Island, Litchfield, and the Georgetown side of Murrells Inlet."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What documents do I need to register a child for school in Horry County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Pre-enrollment is online and asks you to upload four things: a parent or guardian identification card, proof of residency, the student's birth certificate, and the student's immunization records. The school then sends a code to finish registration. A child must be five by September 1 for kindergarten and six by September 1 for first grade."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can my child attend a school we are not zoned for?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Sometimes. Horry County accepts in-district transfer applications through June, does not provide transportation for elective transfers, and denies transfers into schools at or above capacity. Its optional secondary programs are separate: students accepted there are not transfer students and do get transportation. Georgetown County's zones are set under a federal court order, so its transfers are limited to the narrow categories in district policy."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Chapter3 Realty recommend schools?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Fair housing law treats an agent's opinions about schools as a form of steering, and we will not give you a different answer than we would give anyone else. South Carolina publishes a report card for every public school, and both districts publish their own data. This page points you to those sources and to the people who can confirm a zone."}}]}</script>
