ew-construction/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Builders here offer closing cost credits, design money and rate buydowns</a> to buyers who use the builder's preferred lender with an FHA, VA or conventional loan. In Chapter3's experience a buyer with an investor loan, such as a DSCR loan, almost never gets those incentives.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">If a builder offers one on an investor loan, count it as a gain, but not part of the plan. If you need to know what the rates and monthly payments would look like here in Myrtle Beach, call us. We work with our preferred lender to give you solid numbers.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What else changes when the rental is new?</h2><ul style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin:0 0 1rem 1.3rem;padding:0"><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem"><strong>The tax.</strong> The county assesses a rental at 6 percent. <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">The bill is about three times the bill for the same house as a primary residence</a>. That is the same for a new house and an old one.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem"><strong>The dues.</strong> Association dues in a new community often rise once the builder turns the association over to the owners.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem"><strong>The warranty.</strong> Most builders give a written warranty. The usual terms are one year on workmanship and materials, two years on the plumbing, electrical and heating and cooling systems, and ten years on the structure. It starts at closing. In Chapter3's experience many builders also send a repair crew back near the end of the first year. The crew fixes drywall cracks and nail pops and touches up paint. Ask for the warranty booklet before you sign.</li><li style="margin-bottom:.5rem"><strong>The competition.</strong> A new community has many near-identical houses. Several owners rent at the same time, and the builder is still selling new houses on the same street, some with incentives. A tenant compares the houses on price, because the houses are the same. You cannot charge more for a feature every house has, so your rent is the lowest rent on the street. That ends when the build-out ends and the houses start to differ in condition and upgrades.</li></ul><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Buying your first new build as a rental?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the community and the budget. We read the rules, compare the loans, and run the rent before you sign.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="/contact/">Let us make it simple</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">New construction rental FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can I rent out a new construction home in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Usually. It depends on the rules recorded for the community and on the builder's contract. A rule counts only if it is recorded with the county, so we pull the recorded set before you sign.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can an HOA ban rentals in South Carolina?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. A recorded rule that bans or limits renting is enforceable. State law requires the rule to be recorded with the county to count. It does not limit what a recorded rule may say about renting.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Do builders offer incentives to investors?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Rarely. Most incentives go to buyers using the builder's preferred lender with an FHA, VA or conventional loan. In Chapter3's experience an investor loan almost never gets them.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is it better to buy early or late in a new community?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Early, for both cash flow and appreciation. In one Little River community the first townhouse sold for $230,000 and the last for $292,000, about eighteen months apart. The rent stayed a little over $2,000 for both.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What warranty comes with a new construction rental?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most builders give a written warranty. The usual terms are one year on workmanship and materials, two years on the plumbing, electrical and heating and cooling systems, and ten years on the structure. It starts at closing. Ask for the booklet before you sign.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How many new homes are being built around Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Builders were allowed to start 6,898 homes in the Myrtle Beach area in 2025 and 7,152 in 2024, by the federal permit count.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/MYRT845BPPRIV" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census building permits, Myrtle Beach area, on FRED</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t27c030.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SC Code 27-30-130, recording of association rules</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/register-of-deeds/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County Register of Deeds</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/acclaimweb" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County records index</a>, <a href="https://www.strucsure.com/builders/our-builder-warranties/1-2-10-warranty/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The 1-2-10 builder warranty, StrucSure Home Warranty</a>. Read September 7, 2026. Educational only. Rules change; read the recorded set for the community before you sign.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--navy);padding:3rem 0"><div class="wrap" style="text-align:center;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--ivory);margin-bottom:1rem">Read the rules before you sign with the builder.</h2><p style="color:rgba(244,239,232,.75);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:1.6rem">One call. We pull the recorded rules and run the rent.</p><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="tel:+18543332135">Call a specialized agent</a></div></section></main>
