-<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/invest/">Invest</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Section 8 rentals</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Voucher rentals</p><h1 class="detail-h1">How does renting to a Section 8 voucher tenant work in Horry County?<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">The payment standard, the inspection, the contract.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated September 7, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">In Horry County the housing authority pays most of a voucher tenant's rent by direct deposit, up to a payment standard that depends on the bedroom count.</p><div style="margin-top:1.8rem"><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="tel:+18543332135">Call to learn more</a></div></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A Housing Choice Voucher, still called Section 8, pays part of a tenant's rent. Two housing authorities run it in Horry County. The Housing Authority of Myrtle Beach serves its area in the eastern county. The Conway Housing Authority serves Conway and the unincorporated county. The authority pays its share to you by direct deposit each month. The tenant pays the rest. The most the program pays depends on a payment standard for each bedroom count, between 90 and 110 percent of the federal fair market rent. For four bedrooms that rent is $1,981 this fiscal year. The house must pass an inspection first, and the rent must match similar houses nearby. We run the numbers before you offer.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What is a Housing Choice Voucher?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A voucher is federal rent help. A family with low income uses it to rent a house from a private owner. Most people still call it Section 8.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The federal housing agency pays for it. A local housing authority runs it. The family finds the house. You screen the family and rent to them. The authority pays part of the rent to you.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Who</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">What they do</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The family</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Finds the house, signs the lease, pays its share of the rent</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The housing authority</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Inspects the house, checks the rent, pays its share by direct deposit</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">You</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Screen the family, sign the lease and the contract, keep the house to the standard</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The voucher has a bedroom count. <a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-24/section-982.402" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The authority picks it by family size</a>. The family may rent a bigger or a smaller house. The count matters because it caps what the program pays.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The tenant pays a share of the rent from income, usually 30 to 40 percent of adjusted income. The authority pays the rest, up to its cap.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Who runs the program in Horry County?</h2><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Authority</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Vouchers</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Where its vouchers can be used</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Phone</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Housing Authority of Myrtle Beach</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">660</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Its service area, which it describes as eastern Horry County</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">843-918-1525</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Conway Housing Authority</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">373</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The City of Conway and the unincorporated county</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">843-248-7327</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://mbhaonline.org/housing_programs/housing_choice_voucher_program_(hcv)/index.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Myrtle Beach authority</a> is at 1704 North Oak Street. <a href="https://mbhaonline.org/applicants/applicant_information.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Its vouchers work only inside its service area</a>. <a href="https://www.conwayhousingsc.org/housing-choice-vouchers" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Conway authority</a> lists its rules and forms online.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The tenant's voucher names the authority. A Conway voucher rents in Conway or the unincorporated county. A Myrtle Beach voucher rents in that authority's service area. Ask which authority issued the voucher before you take an application.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">How much does a voucher pay?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The program pays up to a payment standard for each bedroom count. <a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-24/section-982.503" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The rule puts the standard between 90 and 110 percent</a> of the federal fair market rent. Each authority picks its own number in that range. Neither authority lists its standards online. Ask for the current table before you price the house.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Bedrooms</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Fair market rent, federal fiscal year 2027</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Studio</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,155</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">One</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,258</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Two</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,504</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Three</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,823</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Four</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,981</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.huduser.gov/portal/datasets/fmr/fmr2027/FY27_FMRs.xlsx" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Those are the federal figures for Horry County</a>, <a href="https://www.huduser.gov/portal/datasets/fmr.html" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">the 40th percentile of rents</a> for standard units with utilities included. At 110 percent, the four-bedroom standard is $2,179.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The standard is the most the program counts toward the rent. The authority pays the standard minus the tenant's share. If you charge more than the standard, the tenant pays the extra.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-24/section-982.505" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The authority uses the lower of two bedroom counts</a>: the count on the voucher and the count of your house. A four-bedroom house earns the four-bedroom standard only for a family with a four-bedroom voucher.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In Chapter3's files a developer from Maryland buys three- and four-bedroom houses here that need work. He fixes them and rents them to voucher families. One house cost $220,000 to buy and repair. It is worth about $280,000 now and rents at the four-bedroom standard. The bedroom count is why he buys the bigger houses.</p><div style="border-left:3px solid var(--brass);background:var(--ivory);padding:1.2rem 1.4rem;margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;margin-bottom:.4rem">Want help buying a house for this strategy?</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:.8rem">Tell us the bedroom count and the budget. We find houses that pass the inspection and fit the payment standard, and run the numbers before you offer.</p><a class="btn btn-brass" href="tel:+18543332135">Call a specialized agent</a></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">How is the rent split between the tenant and the authority?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Enter your rent and the family's income. The tool splits the rent between the authority and the tenant. It also shows which bedroom standards are at or above your rent.</p>
+<main id="main"><div class="detail-hero bg-grid"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/invest/">Invest</a><span>/</span><span style="color:var(--muted)">Section 8 rentals</span></div><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Voucher rentals</p><h1 class="detail-h1">How does renting to a Section 8 voucher tenant work in Horry County?<br/><em style="font-style:italic;color:var(--brass)">The payment standard, the inspection, the contract.</em></h1><p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;margin-bottom:1rem">By <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Devin Day</strong>, Operations Officer &middot; Reviewed by <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">Tim Nash</strong>, Broker-in-Charge &middot; <span style="white-space:nowrap">Updated October 27, 2026</span></p><p class="detail-sub">In Horry County the housing authority pays most of a voucher tenant's rent by direct deposit, up to a payment standard that depends on the bedroom count.</p><div style="margin-top:1.8rem"><a class="btn btn-brass btn-lg" href="tel:+18543332135">Call to learn more</a></div></div></div><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">The short answer</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A Housing Choice Voucher, still called Section 8, pays part of a tenant's rent. Two housing authorities run it in Horry County. The Housing Authority of Myrtle Beach serves its area in the eastern county. The Conway Housing Authority serves Conway and the unincorporated county. The authority pays its share to you by direct deposit each month. The tenant pays the rest. The most the program pays depends on a payment standard for each bedroom count, between 90 and 110 percent of the federal fair market rent. For four bedrooms that rent is $1,981 this fiscal year. The house must pass an inspection first, and the rent must match similar houses nearby. We run the numbers before you offer.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">What is a Housing Choice Voucher?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A voucher is federal rent help. A family with low income uses it to rent a house from a private owner. Most people still call it Section 8.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The federal housing agency pays for it. A local housing authority runs it. The family finds the house. You screen the family and rent to them. The authority pays part of the rent to you.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Who</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">What they do</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The family</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Finds the house, signs the lease, pays its share of the rent</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">The housing authority</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Inspects the house, checks the rent, pays its share by direct deposit</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">You</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Screen the family, sign the lease and the contract, keep the house to the standard</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The voucher has a bedroom count. <a href="https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-24/section-982.402" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The authority picks it by family size</a>. The family may rent a bigger or a smaller house. The count matters because it caps what the program pays.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The tenant pays a share of the rent from income, usually 30 to 40 percent of adjusted income. The authority pays the rest, up to its cap.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Who runs the program in Horry County?</h2><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Authority</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Vouchers</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Where its vouchers can be used</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);