+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Article", "@id": "https://chapter3realty.com/invest/str-tax-treatment/#article", "headline": "Can rental losses reduce the tax on your W-2 income?", "description": "Rental losses normally cannot reduce the tax on a W-2 salary. A short-term rental you run yourself is the exception. The two tests, and why rental pools fail one.", "url": "https://chapter3realty.com/invest/str-tax-treatment/", "author": {"@id": "https://chapter3realty.com/#org"}, "reviewedBy": {"@type": "Person", "name": "Timothy Nash", "alternateName": "Tim Nash", "jobTitle": "Broker-in-Charge"}, "publisher": {"@id": "https://chapter3realty.com/#org"}, "datePublished": "2026-09-04", "dateModified": "2026-10-27", "inLanguage": "en-US", "image": "https://chapter3realty.com/og-image.jpg", "mainEntityOfPage": {"@id": "https://chapter3realty.com/invest/str-tax-treatment/"}, "about": {"@type": "Thing", "name": "Grand Strand short-term rental regulations"}, "keywords": "Airbnb losses offset W-2 income, short-term rental tax loophole, material participation short-term rental, passive loss rules vacation rental, Myrtle Beach rental pool taxes"}</script>
 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "Can I deduct Airbnb losses from my W-2 income?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "For a long-term rental, up to $25,000 of loss can reduce your salary income if you take part in the management decisions and your income is under $100,000. For a short-term rental with average stays of seven days or less, the loss can reduce your salary only if you pass a material participation test."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the seven-day rule?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "If the average guest stay across the year is seven days or less, the property is not a rental activity for tax purposes. It is treated as a business. That removes the automatic passive label. You still need to pass a material participation test."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Do I need to be a real estate professional?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "No. That is a different rule with its own hour requirements. The seven-day route does not use it."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Does a property manager rule me out?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "It makes the tests harder. Several tests compare your hours with everyone else who worked on the property. If the manager worked more hours than you, test 3 fails. If you do not need the loss against your salary, a manager is fine."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What records do I need?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "A calendar, an appointment book, or a written summary of your hours. Daily logs are not required. Start on the day you close."}}]}</script>
