 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "@id": "https://chapter3realty.com/invest/strategies/#faq", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the best real estate investment strategy in Myrtle Beach?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "There is no single best strategy. Short-term rentals fit condos near the beach. Long-term rentals fit the year-round inland areas. BRRRR fits houses that need work, and fix and flip fits houses that just look dated. The right call depends on the property, your cash, your financing, and how hands-on you want to be."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Do I need a lot of cash to invest on the Grand Strand?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The strategy sets the cash you need. Buy-and-hold with a DSCR loan needs a substantial down payment. House hacking, living in one unit of a duplex while tenants rent the rest, can need far less. Fix and flip needs the most cash. Repairs and the monthly bills while you own it come out of pocket or from a short-term loan."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can Chapter3 help with both the property and the financing?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Chapter3 handles the property and our lending partner handles the loan. We run the numbers on the property and work with your lender on the timeline. That matters most on DSCR purchases, BRRRR refinances, and 1031 exchange deadlines, where the property and the loan must move together."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Which strategy works best for out-of-state investors?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Buy-and-hold with a professional property manager is the most common entry point, because it asks the least of your time. Many investors start with a single long-term or short-term rental. They move into BRRRR or small multifamily once they know the market."}}]}</script>
