 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Where are Airbnbs legal on the Grand Strand?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"North Myrtle Beach citywide, subject to the covenants. Myrtle Beach only in the zones marked for it, not in residential neighborhoods. Surfside Beach in two districts. Unincorporated Horry County where the covenants allow. Georgetown County's resort districts, for a house rented up to 30 days."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Murrells Inlet in Horry County or Georgetown County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Georgetown County, along with Litchfield and the southern part of Garden City. Georgetown County requires no business license, and its 3 percent accommodations tax stops at 30 days."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which area is best for a long-term rental?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Conway, Carolina Forest, Socastee and Little River have the lowest prices of entry and year-round tenants. The choice within them comes down to the neighborhood's covenants and the numbers for the house."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I do a 90-day furnished rental in a Myrtle Beach neighborhood?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, in residential zones, because a stay of 90 days or more is not a short-term rental there. Not in the oceanfront buildings covered by the December 2024 overlay."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do the rules change?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Two state bills in committee would either stop local bans or confirm them, and North Myrtle Beach is drafting its own rules. Check the row before you offer."}}]}</script>
