+## Who won the 2026 election in South Carolina?
+Annie Andrews, a Democrat, won the U.S. Senate seat over Darline Graham, the Republican appointed to it in July. She is the first woman elected to represent South Carolina in the U.S. Senate.
+Alan Wilson, a Republican and the state's attorney general, won the governor's race. Jermaine Johnson, the Democrat, conceded on election night.
+South Carolina's 2026 results, unofficial count Race Winner Result How it was decided
+U.S. Senate Winner Annie Andrews (D) Result 51.0% to 46.8% over Darline Graham (R) How it was decided The AP called it on election night. CBS News projected it too.
+Governor Winner Alan Wilson (R), with Mike Reichenbach for lieutenant governor Result 51.7% to 47.0% over Jermaine Johnson (D) How it was decided Johnson conceded on election night.
+U.S. House, 7th District, which includes Horry County Winner Russell Fry (R) Result 56.8% to 43.2% over John Gregory Vincent (D) How it was decided The AP called it.
