+These are unofficial counts until the State Board of Canvassers certifies them. State law requires a recount when a race is within 1 percent. Two House races are that close, so the House split could still move.
+In Washington, CBS News projects that Democrats will control the U.S. Senate in January. Before the election, Republicans held 53 seats to 47.
+
+## How did Horry County vote in 2026?
+Horry County voted more Republican than the state. Darline Graham carried the county with about 60 percent, though she lost statewide. Wilson won it with about 64 percent.
+No question for Horry County, Myrtle Beach, North Myrtle Beach or Surfside Beach was on the ballot. Nothing on the local ballot changed a tax or a rule for homes.
