+### Where a property tax shift was tried before
+Act 388, a state tax law passed in 2006, removed school operating taxes from homes people live in. It added a 1 percent sales tax to make up the money.
+At 4 percent, the yearly bill on a rental inside Myrtle Beach would fall by about a third. In Chapter3's files, property tax stops more rental deals here than insurance does.
