+By Devin Day , Chief Operating Officer, and Abdulla Hijazi , Chief Marketing Officer · Reviewed by Tim Nash , Broker-in-Charge · Updated November 4, 2026
+Federal flood insurance expires Dec. 11, before South Carolina's new senator is sworn in. In a lapse, Grand Strand buyers cannot get a new federal flood policy.
+
+The short answer
+No, not by itself, and not before Dec. 11. Federal flood insurance expires that day, and Annie Andrews takes her U.S. Senate seat in January.
+Congress has kept the program running with 36 short extensions since late 2017, and every lapse so far has ended. Under current law, most flood premiums can rise up to 18% a year, whoever holds the seat. A lasting change needs Congress as a whole, with 60 Senate votes to end debate on a regular bill.
+
