+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Who won the Senate race in South Carolina in 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Annie Andrews, a Democrat, won with about 51 percent of the unofficial count over Darline Graham, a Republican. The AP called the race on election night, and her term begins in January."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who won the governor's race, and is it official?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Alan Wilson, a Republican, won with about 52 percent, and Jermaine Johnson conceded on election night. Every result is unofficial until the State Board of Canvassers certifies it."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will Myrtle Beach home prices go down after the election?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In the year after each election from 2016 to 2024, the Myrtle Beach-area price index rose, by about 3 to 22 percent. In the latest year prices were about flat, up 0.8 percent."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Did anything on the Horry County ballot affect real estate?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. There was no county, city or statewide ballot question. The ballot held only races for office, from Congress and governor to County Council and school board."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can Alan Wilson cut the property tax on rentals by himself?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Changing the 6 percent ratio needs two-thirds of each chamber, 83 House votes and 31 Senate votes. Republicans won 79 House seats in the unofficial count, so a change needs Democratic votes too."}}]}</script>
