 <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much is the HOA fee in The Farm at Carolina Forest?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The HOA fee is $107 a month, or about $1,300 a year. The HOA can raise it by up to 20 percent a year."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is The Farm at Carolina Forest a gated community?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. The Farm is not gated, and its roads are county-owned. Entry to the HOA's pools is by key card."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When was The Farm at Carolina Forest built?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Farm was built in stages, on land D.R. Horton added over the years. Most houses were built from 2004 to 2009, and most of the rest about a decade later."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is The Farm at Carolina Forest in a high-risk flood zone?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Every home in The Farm is outside the high-risk flood zone on the government's flood map. That means federal law does not make your lender require flood insurance. If you want a policy for a house anyway, one in this ZIP code usually costs about $600 a year."}}]}</script>
