ose .c3ph-hero{max-width:640px}.c3-aerial-ctop .c3ph-cr{top:0;bottom:auto;padding:.35rem .6rem 1.6rem 2.6rem;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 0%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0))}@media (max-width:699px){.c3ph-cards>:last-child:nth-child(odd){grid-column:1/-1}}.c3-maps{display:grid;gap:0 1.5rem;max-width:1136px}@media (min-width:900px){.c3-maps{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start}}.c3-maps figure{max-width:none!important;margin:1.4rem 0 .4rem!important}.c3-maps svg,.c3-maps img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.c3-map-links{row-gap:0!important}.c3-map-links a{padding:.55rem 0}ul[role=list][style*="minmax(13rem,1fr)"]{grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(min(13rem,100%),1fr))!important}</style><style>.c3-aerial .c3ph-hero,.c3-aerial-close .c3ph-hero{max-width:720px}</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Conway Medical Center planned a $160 million healthcare facility on the 353 acres along The Farm's north edge. The state bought the land instead, for the <a href="https://www.dnr.sc.gov/news/2025/Jun/jun10-lewisoceanbay.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lewis Ocean Bay Heritage Preserve</a>.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The preserve is home to South Carolina's largest wild population of Venus flytraps, and the new land holds habitat for them too.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem"><a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t51c017.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">State law</a> says a heritage preserve may not be taken for any private use. Once the land is dedicated, that rules out private homes on it. The state has said it will dedicate it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Back inside The Farm, the streets follow its farm theme, from Scarecrow Way to Pumpkin Patch Lane.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-is-a-normal-day-like-in-the-farm-at-carolina-forest"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="A normal day">What is a normal day like in The Farm at Carolina Forest?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">From March through June, a Saturday here can start with a walk in the preserve, among pitcher plants and wildflowers in bloom.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The preserve is open in daylight all year, and the state asks visitors to park and walk its roads. Its main entrance is about 10 minutes by car.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Residents can start a weekday with a workout in the HOA's fitness room, which opens at 5:30 a.m.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A commute to Grand Strand Medical Center, a large hospital, takes about 12 minutes. In our experience, rush hour adds 5 to 10 minutes to the drive times on this page.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The pools stay open until 9 p.m. in season, so there is time for a swim after work. The large pool curves around two small islands of palms, and its wide deck is beside a pond. Owners can also reserve the activity center near it for a private party.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">River Oaks Pizzeria is next to Publix, so dinner and groceries can be one stop.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On a free afternoon, the county library and the <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/departments/parksandrecreation/parks" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Carolina Forest Recreation Center</a> share one campus, about 3 minutes away by car. The center has a rock climbing wall and a full gym.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a longer outing, the county's Bike and Run Park has 7 miles of mountain bike and hiking trails, about 4 minutes by car. Its parking area is a trailhead on the East Coast Greenway, a walking and biking route from Maine to Florida.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="what-are-the-homes-like-in-the-farm-at-carolina-forest"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="The homes">What are the homes like in The Farm at Carolina Forest?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most houses here give you three or four bedrooms and a back yard of your own. A typical lot is about a fifth of an acre.</p><div class="c3-aerial"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/the-farm/the-farm-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/the-farm/the-farm-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/the-farm/the-farm-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="1200" alt="The Farm at Carolina Forest from above, its edge drawn in orange: curving streets of houses around ponds and woods, labelled with the entrance, the activity center, the large pool, The Orchards, the small pool and Planters Point" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>The Farm at Carolina Forest from above. The orange line is the edge of the neighborhood.</figcaption></figure></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Some houses have five bedrooms or more. Most have about 1,450 to 3,200 square feet. Some are one story and some are two.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Orchards has about 200 townhomes, and Planters Point has about 70 condos, most with two or three bedrooms.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Most houses here are about 20 years old. On any house you tour, we check how old the roof and the air conditioner are.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Over the past year, a typical townhome in The Orchards sold for about $230,000, and a condo in Planters Point about $240,000.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="where-is-the-farm-at-carolina-forest"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Where it is">Where is The Farm at Carolina Forest?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Farm is in <a href="/submarkets/carolina-forest/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Carolina Forest</a>, on Carolina Forest Boulevard, outside the Myrtle Beach city limits.</p><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/the-farm/the-farm-where-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/the-farm/the-farm-where-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/the-farm/the-farm-where-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="900" alt="Carolina Forest and Myrtle Beach from above: The Farm outlined in orange, the land set to join the preserve shaded green on its north edge, and labels for Publix, the emergency room 5 minutes away and the beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>Where The Farm is. The drive to the emergency room starts at the entrance nearest the large pool. The orange line is its edge.</figcaption></figure></div><p class="c3-map-links" style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.4rem;margin:.6rem 0 1.6rem;max-width:760px;font-size:.95rem"><span style="color:var(--brass-ink);display:inline-flex"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 21s-7-6.2-7-11.5a7 7 0 0 1 14 0C19 14.8 12 21 12 21z"/><circle cx="12" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/></svg></span><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=33.754869,-78.875215" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open The Farm at Carolina Forest in Google Maps</a></p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Also close by</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Drive</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Tanger Outlets on Highway 501</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 13 minutes</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach Boardwalk, along the ocean</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 15 minutes</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Myrtle Beach International Airport</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 20 minutes</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="which-schools-is-the-farm-at-carolina-forest-zoned-for"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Schools">Which schools is The Farm at Carolina Forest zoned for?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Both Ocean Bay schools are on International Drive at The Farm's edge. A sidewalk runs along Wheatfield Drive to International Drive.</p><div class="c3-aerial c3-aerial-close"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/the-farm/the-farm-school-zones-from-above-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/the-farm/the-farm-school-zones-from-above-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/the-farm/the-farm-school-zones-from-above-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="900" alt="The east side of Carolina Forest from above, with a blue school zone, The Farm outlined in orange inside it, and one dot labelled Ocean Bay Elementary and Ocean Bay Middle" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>The blue area is zoned for Ocean Bay Elementary, Ocean Bay Middle and Carolina Forest High. The Farm, outlined in orange, is inside it. The dot is the two Ocean Bay schools.</figcaption></figure></div><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">School</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Grades</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Drive by car</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Ocean Bay Elementary</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">K to 5</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 6 minutes</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Ocean Bay Middle</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">6 to 8</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 4 minutes</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Carolina Forest High</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">9 to 12</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">About 15 minutes</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We check the <a href="https://hcsd1.maps.arcgis.com/apps/instant/lookup/index.html?appid=72f93a5329c54f54840673fe6430ab43" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">current zones</a> for any home you like. See <a href="/buyers/relocating/schools/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">how school zones work in Horry County</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-does-it-cost-to-live-in-the-farm-at-carolina-forest"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Costs">What does it cost to live in The Farm at Carolina Forest?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a typical house you live in, the HOA fee and the county property tax come to about $2,600 a year.</p><div style="overflow-x:auto;margin:1.2rem 0;max-width:760px"><table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.92rem"><thead><tr><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">Each year, for a $350,000 house you live in</th><th style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);color:var(--navy);text-align:left;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">About</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">HOA fee, $107 a month</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,300</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">County property tax</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$1,300</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">Total</td><td style="padding:.55rem .8rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted)">$2,600</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Cable TV from Spectrum is the largest share of the <a href="https://www.farmatcarolinaforest.com/uploads/documents_page/The%20Farm%20@%20Carolina%20Forest%20HOA%20-%20%20Approved%20Budget%20Summary%20Report.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">fee</a>. The fee also covers landscaping and the ponds, trash pickup and the pools. We confirm with the HOA whether internet is in the fee.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Townhomes in The Orchards and condos in Planters Point pay a second HOA fee as well. Owners in The Orchards pay about $225 to $255 a month in all, and in Planters Point about $450 to $500.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The county adds a stormwater fee of about $90 a year to the tax bill. On an ordinary sale, the buyer pays the HOA a one-time $250 transfer fee at closing.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="what-are-the-pros-and-cons-of-living-in-the-farm-at-carolina"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Pros and cons">What are the pros and cons of living in The Farm at Carolina Forest?</h2><style>.c3-pc{display:grid;gap:1rem;max-width:960px;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem}@media (min-width:760px){.c3-pc{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start}}.c3-pc>div{padding:1.1rem 1.2rem .6rem}.c3-pc h3{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .8rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem}.c3-pc,.c3-pc ul{font-size:1em}.c3-pc ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.c3-pc li{display:flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:flex-start;color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 .9rem}.c3-pc li svg{flex:none;margin-top:.3rem}.c3-pc .c3-pc-do{display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:500;margin-top:.2rem}</style><div class="c3-pc"><div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass)"><h3>Pros</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Woods along the north edge that belong to the state, not a builder.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>The same three public schools for every home, two of them at its edge.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Groceries and dinner out without a long drive.</span></li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--muted)"><h3>Cons</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>The large pool has sunk more than it should, and the HOA board has not decided whether to repair or replace it. The board can vote a one-time charge to owners, called a <a href="/hoa/special-assessments/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">special assessment</a>. <span class="c3-pc-do">We read the board's latest minutes on the pool for you.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Townhomes and condos pay a second HOA fee. <span class="c3-pc-do">We show you both fees side by side for any townhome or condo.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>The preserve allows both hiking and hunting. Deer season runs from mid-September to January 1, and small game to March 1. On burn days, the road to its entrance can close because of the smoke. <span class="c3-pc-do">We show you how far any house is from the preserve's hunting land.</span></span></li></ul></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-are-the-hoa-rules-in-the-farm-at-carolina-forest"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="HOA rules">What are the HOA rules in The Farm at Carolina Forest?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Under the <a href="https://www.farmatcarolinaforest.com/uploads/documents_page/NEW%20Rules%20%26%20Regulations.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HOA rules</a>, owners can rent their homes with a written lease, and the HOA's governing documents have no cap on how many homes are rented.</p><ul role="list" style="list-style:none;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(13rem,1fr));gap:.75rem;max-width:760px"><li style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.9rem .85rem 1rem;margin:0"><span style="display:flex;width:2.6rem;height:2.6rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory-2);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:.6rem"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 21h18M5 21V9.5M19 21V9.5M5 9.5C7 6.8 9.4 5.5 12 5.5s5 1.3 7 4M12 5.5V21M8.5 7v14M15.5 7v14M5 15h14"/></svg></span><strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:.25rem">A fence or shed</strong><span style="display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5">Needs the HOA's approval first, with a land surveyor's drawing of the lot.</span></li><li style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.9rem .85rem 1rem;margin:0"><span style="display:flex;width:2.6rem;height:2.6rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory-2);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:.6rem"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 3v13M12 3l7 11h-7M10 6l-5 8h5M3 16h18l-2 4H5z"/></svg></span><strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:.25rem">Cars and boats</strong><span style="display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5">Cars go in the garage or driveway, not on the street or lawn. A boat, trailer or camper needs the HOA's written approval to stay outside.</span></li><li style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.9rem .85rem 1rem;margin:0"><span style="display:flex;width:2.6rem;height:2.6rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory-2);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:.6rem"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 13c-2.5 0-5 2.6-5 5 0 1.6 1.2 2.5 2.6 2.5.9 0 1.6-.5 2.4-.5s1.5.5 2.4.5c1.4 0 2.6-.9 2.6-2.5 0-2.4-2.5-5-5-5z"/><circle cx="5.3" cy="11" r="1.8"/><circle cx="9" cy="6.3" r="1.8"/><circle cx="15" cy="6.3" r="1.8"/><circle cx="18.7" cy="11" r="1.8"/></svg></span><strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:.25rem">Pets</strong><span style="display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5">Up to three dogs and cats in all. Dogs stay on a leash outside.</span></li><li style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:.9rem .85rem 1rem;margin:0"><span style="display:flex;width:2.6rem;height:2.6rem;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ivory-2);color:var(--brass-ink);align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:.6rem"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M9 15V5a2 2 0 0 0-2-2M15 15V5a2 2 0 0 0-2-2M9 7h6M9 11h6M2 18c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0M2 21.5c1.7 1.2 3.3 1.2 5 0s3.3-1.2 5 0 3.3 1.2 5 0 3.3-1.2 5 0"/></svg></span><strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;font-weight:500;line-height:1.3;margin-bottom:.25rem">The pools</strong><span style="display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem;line-height:1.5">Open April 15 to October 15, with no lifeguard. Up to six guests per home, with the owner there.</span></li></ul><div class="c3-story" style="background:var(--ivory);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);padding:1.5rem 1.5rem .7rem;margin:1.4rem 0 1.4rem;max-width:720px"><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem"><strong>Example:</strong> The house Rachel and Luis found in The Farm has a big back yard, and they picture a pool in it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem">Before they make an offer, their Chapter3 agent reads the HOA rules with them. No lot in The Farm may have a private swimming pool. A hot tub is allowed with the HOA committee's approval.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:640px;margin:0 0 .9rem">Rachel and Luis buy the house anyway. They swim at The Farm's large pool and plan a hot tub for the yard.</p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="was-the-farm-at-carolina-forest-part-of-an-old-bombing-range"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Old bombing range">Was The Farm at Carolina Forest part of an old bombing range?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Yes. From 1942 to 1948, the Army Air Force used the land as a bombing and gunnery range, along with other parts of Carolina Forest. The Army Corps of Engineers has finished the cleanup work on the land under every home in The Farm.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Corps lists Range III, a section that borders The Farm, as under investigation. It touches some of The Farm's open land, but no home lot.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We check the <a href="https://geospatial.sec.usace.army.mil/server/rest/services/Military/FUDS_Data/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Corps' map</a> for every lot we show you. If you ever find something that looks like old ammunition, the <a href="https://www.denix.osd.mil/uxo/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Defense Department's advice</a> is to leave it alone, move away and call 911.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">To compare, see <a href="/buyers/best-neighborhoods/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">the best neighborhoods near Myrtle Beach</a>, <a href="/buyers/gated-communities/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">the gated neighborhoods</a>, <a href="/buyers/no-hoa-homes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">homes with no HOA</a> and <a href="/buyers/affordable-places-to-live/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">the most affordable places to buy</a>.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="the-farm-at-carolina-forest-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">The Farm at Carolina Forest FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How much is the HOA fee in The Farm at Carolina Forest?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The HOA fee is $107 a month, or about $1,300 a year. The HOA can raise it by up to 20 percent a year.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is The Farm at Carolina Forest a gated community?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. The Farm is not gated, and its roads are county-owned. Entry to the HOA's pools is by key card.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">When was The Farm at Carolina Forest built?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The Farm was built in stages, on land D.R. Horton added over the years. Most houses were built from 2004 to 2009, and most of the rest about a decade later.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is The Farm at Carolina Forest in a high-risk flood zone?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Every home in The Farm is outside the high-risk flood zone on the government's flood map. That means federal law does not make your lender require flood insurance. If you want a policy for a house anyway, one in this ZIP code usually costs about $600 a year.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.farmatcarolinaforest.com/uploads/documents_page/The%20Farm%20@%20Carolina%20Forest%20HOA%20-%20%20Approved%20Budget%20Summary%20Report.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HOA budget</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Deed records</a>, <a href="https://hcsd1.maps.arcgis.com/apps/instant/lookup/index.html?appid=72f93a5329c54f54840673fe6430ab43" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">School zones</a>, <a href="https://msc.fema.gov/portal/search?AddressQuery=201%20Carolina%20Farms%20Blvd%2C%20Myrtle%20Beach%2C%20SC%2029579" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA flood map</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">County tax levies</a>, <a href="https://www.dnr.sc.gov/news/2025/Jun/jun10-lewisoceanbay.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDNR preserve</a>, <a href="https://www.scstatehouse.gov/code/t51c017.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Preserve law</a>, <a href="https://geospatial.sec.usace.army.mil/server/rest/services/Military/FUDS_Data/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Corps map</a>, <a href="https://www.denix.osd.mil/arc/dep-arc-fy-2024/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DoD cleanup</a>, <a href="https://www.denix.osd.mil/uxo/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DoD safety</a>. Not legal or tax advice. Sizes, ages and second HOA fees are from listings. Drives start at the Farmers Rest Drive entrance, without traffic. The flood cost is FEMA's middle policy in ZIP 29579. Corps status: fiscal year 2024.</p><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">The Farm at Carolina Forest from above. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty drew the outline from Horry County GIS parcels, added six labels placed from county data and adjusted the colors.</div><div role="listitem">Where The Farm is. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty drew The Farm's outline from Horry County GIS parcels, shaded the state's 353-acre tract from the same parcels, added seven labels placed from county data and ledger rows, and adjusted the colors.</div><div role="listitem">The blue area is zoned for Ocean Bay Elementary, Ocean Bay Middle and Carolina Forest High. U.S. government aerial photo, 2023, by the USDA Farm Service Agency, <a href="https://www.fsa.usda.gov/help/policies-and-links/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://imagery.nationalmap.gov/arcgis/rest/services/USGSNAIPImagery/ImageServer" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The National Map (USGS)</a>. Chapter3 Realty drew The Farm's outline from Horry County GIS parcels, shaded the area inside all three of Horry County Schools' 2025 to 2026 attendance zones for Ocean Bay Elementary, Ocean Bay Middle and Carolina Forest High, added three labels placed from that data and county address points, and adjusted the colors.</div><div role="listitem">Chapter3 Realty resized these photos and cropped some of them.</div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/buyers/the-farm/the-farm-from-above-1200w.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/buyers/the-farm/the-farm-from-above-1200w.webp","width":1200,"height":1200,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","name":"The Farm at Carolina Forest from above","ca